Z||000008||Monkeyman||08-29-2000||12:15 AM||||Nope.  Not whipped.  (Well, sorta.  But in a good way.  I'd do almost anything for Monkeygal, but she'd do the same for me, too.)<P>Here's the story.  The Monkeymobile never ran well, but she always ran.  Had a small oil leak, though.  I checked the oil daily and added about a 1/2 quart every 3 days or so.  One day I decided that I just <I>had</I> to pull the sunroof out and catch some breeze.  No problem.  I pulled the sunroof out the next day, too.  That night (after checking the oil again) I lost most of my oil and lunched the motor.  I figure it this way.  The Monkeymobile just didn't like having the sunroof out and that's why she passed away.  Moral of the story?  I <B>NEVER</B> drive with the sunroof out of the Grape Ape.  This way the motor will last until I can afford to upgrade.  (Either summer of '01 or '02.)  My wife forbid me to ever remove the sunroof.  I just happen to agree with her.  If you were me, after hearing my story, would you want to take the chance and drive with your sunroof out?  I think not. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
